{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And the waters diminished.</b> Rashi explained: from the end of a hundred and fifty days the waters began to diminish, and this was on the first of Sivan. How so? On the twenty-eighth of Kislev the rains ceased — that makes three days of Kislev etc. This shows that Rashi holds that the twenty-eighth of Kislev is not counted among the forty days of the rains' descent, but rather it is counted among the hundred and fifty days of the waters' surge. But above, by 'the rain was upon the earth forty days,' Rashi holds that the twenty-eighth of Kislev is counted among the forty days of the rains' descent, as Rashi explained — the first day is not counted in the reckoning because its night is not with it, since it is written 'in the second month, on the seventeenth day of the month, the fountains burst open' etc. — so forty complete days conclude on the twenty-eighth of Kislev. Therefore it is proper to weigh Rashi's opinion thus: 'the first day is not counted in the reckoning' — the meaning is not that the first day of the forty days of rain, which is the seventeenth of Marcheshvan, is excluded from the reckoning of the other days, for the others have their nights with them and this one does not have its night with it; nonetheless it is counted among the forty days of rain. And in this order you will find them to reconcile Rashi: the seventeenth of Marcheshvan was the first of the forty days of rain and its night was not with it, and twelve remaining of Marcheshvan and twenty-seven of Kislev — their nights were with them — and the night of the twenty-eighth of Kislev completes the day of the seventeenth of Marcheshvan that did not have its night with it. So you have forty complete days, from dawn of the seventeenth of Marcheshvan until dawn of the twenty-eighth of Kislev, and thus it is written 'the rain was upon the earth forty days and forty nights.' But the hundred and fifty days of the waters' surge need not be counted as complete days with nights, since it is written 'from the end of a hundred and fifty days' — that is, from dawn of the twenty-eighth of Kislev until nightfall of the first of Sivan. And if you wish to count the hundred and fifty days as complete, nights with days, count them from dawn of the twenty-eighth of Kislev until dawn of the first of Sivan, and they will be a hundred and fifty days and a hundred and fifty complete nights. And if one were to object to Rashi: who required him to count the night of the twenty-eighth of Kislev among the forty days of rain, and the day among the hundred and fifty days — what difference does it make if the day is counted with its night among the forty days? Sivan would still be the seventh month for the cessation. Rather, this is the reason: if you count it among the forty days you will not find 'the ark rested in the seventh month on the seventeenth day of the month,' but rather on the eighteenth of the month. How so? Two days of Kislev and a hundred and forty-seven of Tevet, Shevat, Adar, Nisan, Iyar, and one of Sivan — that makes a hundred and fifty complete days, ending at the close of the first of Sivan. The next day the waters began to diminish four cubits for thirty-six days, and when the thirty-six days were completed from when the waters began to diminish, the ark rested on the eighteenth of the month, but it is written 'the ark rested on the seventeenth day of the month.' Nor will you find 'on the first day, the first of the month, the waters dried up.' How so? On the second of Sivan the waters began to diminish, and from there count sixty days for the diminution of the fifteen cubits of water until the tops of the mountains appeared, and from there sixty more days until the dispatch of the dove's last mission, and you will find they conclude on the third of Tishrei, but it is written 'on the first day, the first of the month, the waters dried up.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:36.624587087Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}